  "authorship": "Compact: body region remap shortens rear overhang and wheelbase, lowers cabin and flares fenders; rigid donor wheel assemblies, a thin conformal front lip and moulded ducktail sampled from actual donor bumper/boot contours, plus flush hood vents. Wagon: donor upper roof/pillars/glazing and boot remapped by one monotone Z profile, retaining original Y heights and producing a longer roof, coherent steep rear screen and compressed boot deck. Thin rails raycast the actual high donor shell and sit on short attached mounts. Patrol: donor body exact except explicit rigid wheel Y corrections that resolve inherited unequal ground contacts; normals/UVs/triangles unchanged. All3include a batched chamfered six-chamber lightbar and two roofmounts."
